@startuml
title 4B - The PR sweep: the safety net\nThe Scheduler only ticks; the adapter reads; the machine decides

skinparam defaultTextAlignment left
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

participant "Scheduler" as SCH
participant "GitHubAdapter" as GA
participant "Orchestrator" as O
participant "Store" as S
participant "SandboxPool" as P
participant GitHub

SCH -> O: tick, per configured repo
O -> GA: list open PRs
GA -> GitHub: every open PR
return number, head branch, draft
GA -> O: onPrDiscovered per PR

note right of O
  The sweep only reports facts. Whether a PR is ours is
  the machine's call, by branch prefix.
end note

loop per PR
  O -> S: instance for pr:repo#n?
  return instance + state, or none

  alt none, our branch, not a draft
    O -> S: create PrMaintainer instance
    return prm_pending
    O -> P: enqueue SandboxRun(PrMaintainer)
  else none, somebody else's or still a draft
    O -> O: nothing opened
  else prm_waiting and there is work (unresolved threads, failed CI)
    O -> S: state
    return prm_pending
    O -> P: enqueue SandboxRun(PrMaintainer)
  else prm_waiting and nothing to do
    O -> S: no change
    return prm_waiting
  else prm_attempts_exhausted
    O -> S: no change
    return prm_attempts_exhausted
    note right of O: gave up on purpose, the sweep must not nudge it forever
  else prm_working
    O -> S: no change
    return a run is already live
  end
end

note right of O
  This is also how a missed webhook is recovered.
end note
@enduml
